# WP-D14 golden permission matrix — the documented per-principal-class model (②).
#
# This is the FROZEN written-down source of truth, transcribed from the
# whitepaper §7 product surface (per-principal command verbs) and §3 principal
# model. The acceptance oracle (tests/acceptance_d14.rs) asserts that
# `authz::matrix(class, endpoint)` agrees with EVERY cell here — golden, exact.
#
# Format: one cell per line, `<principal_class> <endpoint> <ALLOW|DENY>`.
# Principal classes: human · orchestrator · worker · model.
# Endpoints:         push · land · undo · policy.
#
# Rationale:
#   push   — universal git verb (§7 "Everyone … every git command"); all allowed.
#   land   — orchestrator's integration verb (§7 Orchestrator: `land`).
#   undo   — human stakeholder control (§7 Human: `undo`).
#   policy — human stakeholder control (§7 Human: `policy`).
# Every non-ALLOW cell is DENY, fail-closed; unrecognized principals are DENY.

human         push    ALLOW
human         land    DENY
human         undo    ALLOW
human         policy  ALLOW

orchestrator  push    ALLOW
orchestrator  land    ALLOW
orchestrator  undo    DENY
orchestrator  policy  DENY

worker        push    ALLOW
worker        land    DENY
worker        undo    DENY
worker        policy  DENY

model         push    ALLOW
model         land    DENY
model         undo    DENY
model         policy  DENY
